(5450136, 782671, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by VitaminB:</b></div><hr/><i>Thanks for your comment. I can appreciate the fact that this is essentially a photo of artwork... but it essentially no different than the photo which inspired it, <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=81530" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jeger</a>''s Mona Lisa:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=765389" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/994/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_765389.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/994/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_765389.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/994/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_765389.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>While I am not bothered by my score overall, I am really happy with it, I did get a lot of low votes, which the Mona Lisa shot didnt get. ...</i></td></tr></table> <br/>The difference between the Mona Lisa shot and yours is that the Mona Lisa photo has some context and depth to it.  By the photographer including himself with the artwork, plus the wall, baseboard, carpet, etc...it becomes a photo, rather than a direct representation of artwork only.  Again, JMO.</td>', 'Originally posted by VitaminB:Thanks for your comment. I can appreciate the fact that this is essentially a photo of artwork... but it essentially no different than the photo which inspired it,  jeger''s Mona Lisa:  While I am not bothered by my score overall, I am really happy with it, I did get a lot of low votes, which the Mona Lisa shot didnt get. ... The difference between the Mona Lisa shot and yours is that the Mona Lisa photo has some context and depth to it.  By the photographer including himself with the artwork, plus the wall, baseboard, carpet, etc...it becomes a photo, rather than a direct representation of artwork only.  Again, JMO.', '2009-04-23 17:06:54.000000', NULL, 0),
